<title>USA: Lexington B &amp; L Q1 December 31 net rises.</title>
<headline>Lexington B &amp; L Q1 December 31 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mo. 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months</p>
<p>					    1996	   1995</p>
<p> Total interest income	   $ 1,160	 $  970</p>
<p> Total interest expense		600	    575</p>
<p>   Net interest income		 560	    395</p>
<p>Net interest income after</p>
<p>    provision for loan losses	559	    395</p>
<p> Non-interest income		    20	     28</p>
<p> Non-interest expense		  258	    203</p>
<p>   Income before income tax	  321	    220</p>
<p> Income tax expense		    116	     69</p>
<p> Net income				205	    151</p>
<p> Net income per share		 0.18	    N/A</p>
<p>			   (Dollars in thousands)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is Lexington B &amp; L Financial Corp.</p>
<p>Total assets = $61.65 million (Dec 31) vs $61.67 million (Sept 30)</p>
<p>Net loans = $45.38 million (Dec 31) vs $45.35 million (Sept 30)</p>
<p>Deposits = $42.34 million (Dec 31) vs $42.24 million (Sept 30)</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
